config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_IR_CLIMATE_CONTROLLER
	bool "Domoticz plugin: Tasmota IR climate controller"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		Control of IR air conditioners and heat pumps through a Tasmota
		IR bridge: the plugin talks to a Tasmota device with an IR LED
		(an ESP8266/ESP32 with the IRremoteESP8266 firmware, or a
		commercial IR bridge flashed with Tasmota) and sends the
		IR commands of the selected air conditioner model.

		It works for devices that have no Wi-Fi interface of their own,
		which is typical of split air conditioners: the climate device in
		Domoticz (mode, fan speed, temperature setpoint, swing) is
		translated into IR codes by Tasmota, so no cloud account and no
		vendor app are involved.

		The plugin uses only the Domoticz module and the Python standard
		library, and its labels follow the language of the hardware entry
		(17 translations).

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> add the IR climate controller, enter
		the IP address of the Tasmota device and select the air
		conditioner model.

		Upstream publishes no license file, so the plugin keeps the
		licensing status upstream gave it; the build fetches a pinned
		commit of the main branch because there are no release tags.
